CM_ BO_ 790 "Primary engine frame, 10 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 790 EngineSpeed "CONFIDENCE A (confirmed): matched byte-exact against external ground truth. Engine speed. Confirmed on the 2026-06-13 petrol capture against an OBD reading, and again on the 2026-08-20 CNG car: idle median 929 rpm against 931 on a Teltonika FMB001, with a clean 905-5386 rpm sweep in the dedicated rev capture. Measured on this vehicle.";
CM_ BO_ 1366 "Secondary engine-speed broadcast, 10 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1366 EngineSpeed2 "CONFIDENCE A (confirmed): matched byte-exact against external ground truth. Second engine-speed broadcast. Tracks ECM_Engine.EngineSpeed to under 1 rpm at idle and within 6 rpm across a full rev sweep. Measured on this vehicle.";
CM_ BO_ 1456 "Odometer, 1000 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1456 Odometer "CONFIDENCE A (confirmed): matched byte-exact against external ground truth. Odometer, 0.1 km per count. CONFIRMED BY MOTION on the CNG sibling: across a recorded drive the raw went 402419 -> 402430, i.e. 40241.9 -> 40243.0 km, and the cluster photos either side read 40241 and 40243 - the display floors to whole km, so both integers are reproduced. Note the trap: dividing the DISPLAYED 2 km by 11 counts gives a bogus 0.18 km/count. Measured on this vehicle.";
CM_ BO_ 512 "Vehicle speed, 10 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 512 VehicleSpeed "CONFIDENCE A (confirmed): matched byte-exact against external ground truth. Vehicle speed. Integrated over the moving session it gives 1.16 km against the 1.10 km the odometer recorded - inside the odometer's own quantisation (11 counts of 0.1 km carries about +/-9 %). Peak 35.4 km/h, agreeing with the four wheel speeds to 0.2 km/h. Reads exactly 0 in every stationary capture. The scale is corroborated a second way: the four wheel-speed fields on 0x386 (documented in the RE record, not shipped here) integrate to 1.150, 1.148, 1.143 and 1.136 km over the same drive and peak within 0.3 km/h of this signal - four independent sensors agreeing.";
CM_ BO_ 809 "Pedal switches, 10 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 809 BrakePedal "CONFIDENCE B (corroborated): isolated by a controlled experiment or forced by unambiguous physical behaviour; no external number to check against. Set during the five brake presses of the brake-pedal capture. It also moves in the parking-brake capture, which is correct rather than contradictory - the foot brake is pressed while setting the handbrake. Quiet in the other eleven captures.";
CM_ SG_ 809 ClutchPedal "CONFIDENCE B (corroborated): isolated by a controlled experiment or forced by unambiguous physical behaviour; no external number to check against. Ten transitions in the clutch capture, two in the gear capture, and EXACTLY ZERO in all eleven others. Moving in both of those is the confirmation, not a weakness: the clutch has to be pressed to change gear.";
CM_ BO_ 399 "Body status, 10 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 399 ParkingBrake "CONFIDENCE B (corroborated): isolated by a controlled experiment or forced by unambiguous physical behaviour; no external number to check against. Reads 1 through the first four captures, changes during the parking-brake capture, and reads 0 for every capture after - released during that test and left off. 1 = engaged.";
CM_ SG_ 399 AcCompressorOn "CONFIDENCE B (corroborated): isolated by a controlled experiment or forced by unambiguous physical behaviour; no external number to check against. Toggles five times in the AC capture. It also blips once during the parking-brake capture, consistent with the compressor cycling on its own thermostat.";
CM_ BO_ 1345 "Doors and lighting, 100 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1345 HeadlampOn "CONFIDENCE B (corroborated): isolated by a controlled experiment or forced by unambiguous physical behaviour; no external number to check against. Five clean on/off cycles in the headlamp capture and 0 in every one of the other twelve. The cleanest isolation in this pack.";
CM_ SG_ 1345 DoorOpenDriver "CONFIDENCE B (corroborated): isolated by a controlled experiment or forced by unambiguous physical behaviour; no external number to check against. Steps 0/1 in the driver-door capture and is 0 elsewhere. Bit 2 of the same byte is set in three earlier captures and was never isolated - byte 1 is a door bitfield of which only the driver bit is identified.";
CM_ BO_ 1170 "CNG level candidate, 50 ms. UNCONFIRMED - see the signal comment before use.";
CM_ SG_ 1170 CngLevelCandidate "CONFIDENCE C (inferred): structural inference only. Layout is plausible; scale and/or mapping are UNVERIFIED - do not trust the number. UNCONFIRMED - the name says Candidate on purpose. Raw 56 reads 87.5 % on a 0-64 scale against the 86 % a Teltonika FMB001 reported for this bi-fuel car (OBD PID 2F reports the ACTIVE fuel, which was CNG). It is the only UNEXPLAINED byte that fits: of 145 bytes constant across all seventeen captures, exactly three land in the 84-88 % window under any plausible full scale, and the other two are already identified as something else - 0x5B0 byte 1 is part of the odometer and 0x329 byte 4 carries the brake bit. AGAINST IT: this byte did not move by a single count in 33 minutes of running on CNG, and a real gauge at this resolution should have sagged about 2 counts; the rest of the frame (40 FE 0F 00 00 38 00) also looks like fixed configuration. THE TEST: watch it while the CNG tank actually empties. If it does not fall, it is not the gauge - delete it.";
CM_ BO_ 1351 "Seatbelt, 100 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 1351 DriverSeatbeltUnfastened "CONFIDENCE C (inferred): structural inference only. Layout is plausible; scale and/or mapping are UNVERIFIED - do not trust the number. Changes in the seatbelt capture but also in six others - which is what a belt does when people get in and out for the door tests, so it is consistent rather than isolated. POLARITY IS NOT ESTABLISHED.";

